From: Anaconda Inc. <maintainers@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Skip the Z3 soname rewrite when Z3_LIBRARY is not set

Z3_LIBRARY is only defined by the pip-layout FindZ3 module (USE_PYPI_Z3=ON).
With config-mode z3 (conda Z3Config.cmake / z3::libz3) the library already
carries a proper soname; patchelf --print-soname with an empty variable
aborts configure with 'Failed to get Z3 soname using patchelf'.

--- a/3rdparty/tvm/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/3rdparty/tvm/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -566,7 +566,9 @@
     )
   else()
     find_program(PATCHELF_EXECUTABLE patchelf)
-    if (PATCHELF_EXECUTABLE)
+    # Z3_LIBRARY is only set by the pip-layout FindZ3; config-mode z3 (conda)
+    # already has a correct soname and needs no rewrite.
+    if (PATCHELF_EXECUTABLE AND Z3_LIBRARY)
       execute_process(
         COMMAND ${PATCHELF_EXECUTABLE} --print-soname ${Z3_LIBRARY}
         OUTPUT_VARIABLE Z3_SONAME
